abstract: >
  Reproducibility package supporting the paper "Benchmarking Digital Health
  Governance in the WHO European Region: A Composite Maturity Index for
  Cross-Country Policy Comparison" (Curiello, Iannuzzi & Nigro, 2026,
  Benchmarking: An International Journal). The package contains the complete
  R pipeline for constructing the Digital Health Maturity Index (DHMI) — a
  composite benchmarking instrument that quantifies national digital health
  governance maturity across the 53 Member States of the WHO European Region
  using 74 WHO-standardised policy indicators across 10 domains. Components:
  (i) raw WHO 2023 survey data; (ii) R scripts implementing the four-procedure
  robustness protocol (weight perturbation, PCA-derived weighting, missing-data
  sensitivity, external validity testing against DESI 2023 and WHO UHC 2023);
  (iii) k-means cluster analysis pipeline (k=3, validated by silhouette and
  Dunn index); (iv) Spearman correlation analysis with Benjamini-Hochberg FDR
  correction across 903 indicator pairs; (v) LASSO regression with 10-fold and
  leave-one-out cross-validation; (vi) Mann-Whitney U tests with FDR correction
  and effect-size quantification; (vii) renv lockfile for long-term R version
  pinning. The full pipeline reproduces all figures, tables and statistics of
  the paper from raw data in under 15 seconds via a single command
  (Rscript code/run_all.R).

